.TH RSID3 1 "2026-11-24" "rsid3-1.0.0" ""
.SH NAME
rsid3 - list and edit ID3v2 tags
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B rsid3
.RI [ OPTION ]...
.RI [ ACTION ]...
.RI [ FILE ]...
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B rsid3
reads or writes ID3v2 tags in mp3 files. It has partial support for ID3v2.2, ID3v2.3 and ID3v2.4.
.P
If executed without specifying any actions,
.B rsid3
by default prints all frames that it finds in every
.IR FILE .
.P
Otherwise, actions are executed in the order in which they were passed on every
.IR FILE .
This allows for chaining many actions for many files in a single command, which
is intentional design.
.P
Existing tags are never converted to different versions, unless an explicit
action is used. For new tags, ID3v2.4 is the default.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.RB \-h , " \-\-help"
Prints this help message.
.TP
.RB \-V , " \-\-version"
Prints version information.
.TP
.RB \-L , " \-\-list-frames"
Lists all supported frames. See also
.B FRAMES
section.
.TP
.RB "\-d SEP" , " \-\-frame-sep SEP"
Sets the frame separator to SEP (default: "\\n").
.TP
.RB "\-D SEP" , " \-\-file-sep SEP"
Sets the file separator to SEP (default: "\\n").
.TP
.RB \-0d , " \-\-frame-sep-null"
Sets the frame separator to the null byte.
.TP
.RB \-0D , " \-\-file-sep-null"
Sets the file separator to the null byte.
.SH ACTIONS
Actions are a subcategory of options, and are listed separately only for the
sake of convenience.
.TP
.RI "\-\-FRAME [" DESC "] [" LANG ]
Prints the value of FRAME. FRAME can be any ID3v2 frame identifier
(see
.B FRAMES
section).
.IP
The frames TXXX, WXXX, TXX and WXX require a second argument: DESC.
The frames COMM, USLT, COM and ULT require second and third arguments: DESC and LANG.
.IP
If the value of LANG is unknown in advance or irrelevant, "first" can be passed
instead, in which case the first frame with a matching DESC is targeted. Note
that actions modifying the tag may change the order of the frames and affect
what is "first".
.TP
.RI "\-\-FRAME= [" DESC "] [" LANG "] TEXT"
Sets the value of FRAME to TEXT. FRAME can be any ID3v2 frame identifier
(see
.B FRAMES
section).
.IP
The frames TXXX, WXXX, TXX and WXX require a third argument: DESC.
The frames COMM, USLT, COM and ULT require third and fourth arguments: DESC and LANG.
.IP
If the value of LANG is unknown in advance or irrelevant, "first" can be passed
instead, in which case the first frame with a matching DESC is targeted. If no
frame with a matching DESC is found, nothing is set. Note that actions modifying
the tag may change the order of the frames and affect what is "first".
.TP
.RI "\-\-FRAME- [" DESC "] [" LANG ]
Deletes FRAME. FRAME can be any ID3v2 frame identifier
(see
.B FRAMES
section).
.IP
The frames TXXX, WXXX, TXX and WXX require a second argument: DESC.
The frames COMM, USLT, COM and ULT require second and third arguments: DESC and LANG.
.IP
If the value of LANG is unknown in advance or irrelevant, "first" can be passed
instead, in which case the first frame with a matching DESC is targeted. Note
that actions modifying the tag may change the order of the frames and affect
what is "first".
.TP
--id3v2.2, --id3v2.3, --id3v2.4
Convert tags to the requested version of ID3v2. The conversion shall be lossless,
or fail if it is not possible to preserve all information.
.TP
--force-id3v2.2, --force-id3v2.3, --force-id3v2.4
Convert tags to the requested version of ID3v2. The conversion shall always
succeed, but any frames that cannot be converted to the target version shall be
removed.
.TP
--purge-id3v2.2, --purge-id3v2.3, --purge-id3v2.4
Purge tags of the requested version, if present.
.TP
--purge-all
Purge all ID3 tags, if present. Note that this also purges ID3v1 tags.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.IP 0
Success.
.IP 1
Success, but at least one frame was missing. This exit code can only appear
when using print and delete actions. For example, 'rsid3 --TIT2- file.mp3'
shall exit with 0 iff TIT2 got deleted and with 1 iff it was already absent
from file.mp3. With print actions, the behavior is the same and it is the only
way to tell apart a missing frame from an empty string. If multiple frames or
files are concerned, the value is 0 iff all of them existed in all files.
.IP 2
Success, but at least one file did not have a tag. This code can only appear
when invoking the command without any actions.
.IP 255
Invalid arguments.
.IP 254
Failed to execute the specified action.
.SH FRAMES
This section lists all ID3v2 frames and specifiess the level of support
available in
.BR rsid3 .
This information can also be obtained with the "--list-frames" option.
